.TH GIT-SYNC 1 "2026-11-10" "git-sync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-sync \- update all local branches from their remotes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-sync
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-sync
fetches and prunes the remote whose
.I <remote>/HEAD
ref exists (usually
.BR origin ),
then walks every local branch.
A branch that is behind its upstream, or behind the same-named branch on that
remote, is fast-forwarded.
A branch whose upstream was deleted is removed only with
.BR \-\-prune ,
and only if its changes are in the default branch, whether merged, rebased,
or squashed (requires git 2.40 or newer).
Without
.BR \-\-prune ,
no branch is ever deleted.
.PP
Branches with unpushed commits, and deleted branches that are not merged,
are left alone and reported with a warning.
.PP
Tags are neither fetched nor pruned.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-prune
Delete merged branches whose upstream is gone.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ git sync
Updated branch main (was 8915328).
warning: 'feature-123' was deleted on origin
$ git sync --prune
Deleted branch feature-123 (was 7c24329).
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-fetch (1)
